    "conclusion": "Allocating the blanket to Rowan is provisionally preferable because the principle that permits it is harder for anyone to reasonably reject: it avoids an 80-point survival loss to Rowan at the cost of a 60-point loss and promise breach to Sasha. The promise adds moral weight but is not enough to overturn the larger life-and-death stake.",
    "strongest_objection": "Sasha can still reasonably complain that she faces certain death plus a betrayal of trust under action A.",
    "answer_to_objection": "While the broken promise intensifies Sasha’s complaint, contractualist assessment allows weight to the magnitude of expected life loss. Rowan’s larger loss if B is chosen makes promise-keeping reasonably rejectable, provided Ellis conveys sincere regret and an explanation to Sasha.",
    "reversal_condition": "If Sasha’s survival chance with the blanket were equal to or greater than Rowan’s (e.g., also 80% or higher), promise-keeping could no longer be outweighed, and giving the blanket to Sasha would become defensible.",
    "residual_disagreement": [
      "Whether a 20-percentage-point survival gap is sufficient to override a specific promise remains contestable among reasonable parties."
    ]
